[[:db/retract 17592186167170 :question/answer-fields 17592186304239] {:db/id 17592186166902 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e611e5f-9b0f-54fb-976f-649d34b87a37"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166523 :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot t+(-2) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{2}+5\\cdot t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n![](images/4d/4dd9b46275644b83a7aa7ab9f9eaf14a8792442e07c4c4fd3a84a296f1fc2ccd.svg)\nwhere ![](images/96/96e96bf02a2ba8f46452e9ef33bcc6215b1b0696c4e1c6262c1400215857839a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47fd4ff4-6ba7-5ef0-9848-b6ea043ad002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166522 :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ee/ee9461106f5c5b7de1ab9871852a1dcc5042947b635ffe10aba17286dac7124a.svg)\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/90/906d3f915ddca1fae48aa190a0a84236a91b50d5760db43816b1b72f20a4c52c.svg)\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t),$ where $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution $\\mathbf{x}_p(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/97/9790c520e0752c38ac78a0b0266f7b6da292e4db16a353f34a902b587a4e688c.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n![](images/3d/3db9994bc0cab42e973fae4fa0b6f94ce880aa052707d11826fe94f6f75095ad.svg)\nwhere $a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2$ are constants that are to be determined." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0f0ab548-1239-59aa-8a8e-1144624f4ff6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166520 :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ea/ea1c45c30bc57d8f04e7bba3e30a33884899fffd0fb712032595ee742a72704c.svg)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/c3/c3be7834b927a4b8ba684899ee4e617a752ca3f5e09f10a320552fc7f497fb32.svg)\nFind the general solution of the system." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/6c/6c0f164deb5815fc1c79e3dd724b6725168213938a81089867f4343cb4f05974.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/5d/5dc5186154c40546a088db1890991e83c6f594d0042866ae9b86cddb3f2d08d8.svg)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](images/fa/fad28fb44ef22f703cbc8bd6a07d7d35e4a77ffe4fb3cd0ec5fdd3b107317a1b.svg)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 7[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1=7a \\\\ b-3=7b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](images/29/29dcb07dde2cdecb330fddb6168319527336ed7a217506727aa6c28241e32a4c.svg)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](images/3e/3e1b5e881fb3c6d5688fd4978ed0fcc16aec5c6e105c11b919a6a9810762d698.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ce5740c3-890f-53a3-a4fc-da96721e3367" "question-0c85ab3b-11e0-5a86-bc49-d13f4a9dbbcf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166521 :question/problem "![](images/19/192b8b3ce80dafb1a2db21822dad5b477cef90793305284210797cba32536a9f.svg)\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n![](images/55/55f17316cc2c0c5965b1d01598bceec9c2c472d6f6c949a099e65b778e6659e4.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n![](images/e6/e6793e6bbadc20520b14292e048050c850340a535d2ade61a84d5235884794fa.svg)\nwhere $c_1,c_2$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2.$ Substituting $t = 0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-0+4 \\\\ -{0}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4=6 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $c_1 = 2.$ From the second equation, we have $c_2 = -1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](images/bc/bcd9c686f0b6924614b0fadf4d86f7872f3fa33837aedfa0f89c15e9720a8f45.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e611e5f-9b0f-54fb-976f-649d34b87a37" :question/id #uuid "8e611e5f-9b0f-54fb-976f-649d34b87a37" :question/math-academy-id "q-332581" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+2{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)+{t}^{2}+4t-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\,{t}^{2}\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-6}} | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  | {{field-9}} |  |  | {{field-10}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {t}^{2}+(-1)\\cdot t+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-2)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+1\\cdot {t}^{2}+4\\cdot t+(-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd2dd150-cbf8-5943-a9f9-3a6a93823e7c" "answer-field-bdb32997-b396-5479-a6c7-e6c8e9fe8863" "answer-field-d8004ce8-f686-515e-87d2-bc8d64c969f4" "answer-field-7f9e3424-0094-5529-81ab-75fde54feeb3" "answer-field-a1d27ed5-7c3e-593a-b08f-9d0873b77e48" "answer-field-7662e400-ea42-5dea-838f-39937c15e5a3" "answer-field-dc59ec9a-09f3-518e-b59e-bbc9843619e5" "answer-field-5246fc34-6ab2-5f9f-b9da-e96c832c47b6" "answer-field-d66d3d88-f79f-5931-b178-86065afd3933" "answer-field-5f29fb48-ed4b-52ad-b77b-99f62ab2bfc4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd2dd150-cbf8-5943-a9f9-3a6a93823e7c" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd2dd150-cbf8-5943-a9f9-3a6a93823e7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c3cff4d8-918f-53b3-942b-69a690472772" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3cff4d8-918f-53b3-942b-69a690472772"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3cff4d8-918f-53b3-942b-69a690472772" :answer/id #uuid "c3cff4d8-918f-53b3-942b-69a690472772" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bdb32997-b396-5479-a6c7-e6c8e9fe8863" :answer-field/id #uuid "bdb32997-b396-5479-a6c7-e6c8e9fe8863" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9af52ccb-ff3f-5161-8b9f-72c1c3786af6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9af52ccb-ff3f-5161-8b9f-72c1c3786af6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]